    "body": "What you have so far looks good:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlet device = await navigator.hid.requestDevice({filters:[]});\r\nawait device.open();\r\nif (device.opened)\r\n  console.log(\"Device is open.\");\r\n```\r\n\r\nA minor suggestion, consider providing a vendor/product ID filter so the chooser only displays the LUFA device:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlet vendorProductFilter = { vendorId: 0x03eb, productId: 0x204f };\r\nlet device = await navigator.hid.requestDevice({filters:[vendorProductFilter]});\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo send an output report to the device:\r\n\r\n```\r\n// Set reportId to zero if the device does not use report IDs.\r\nlet reportId = 0;\r\n// Create the report buffer.\r\nlet reportData = new Uint8Array([1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0]);\r\n// Send the report.\r\nawait device.sendReport(reportId, reportData);\r\n```\r\n\r\nTo register an input report listener:\r\n\r\n```\r\ndevice.oninputreport = (event) => {\r\n  console.log('Received input report with ID ' + event.reportId + ' from ' + event.device.productName);\r\n  console.log(new Uint8Array(event.data.buffer));\r\n};\r\n```",
